## Function Signature

The function takes an event sender, feedback category, optional rollout path, optional auto-review filename, a Windows sandbox log flag, and a reference to `FeedbackDiagnostics`:

```rust
pub(crate) fn feedback_upload_consent_params(
    app_event_tx: AppEventSender,
    category: FeedbackCategory,
    rollout_path: Option<std::path::PathBuf>,
    auto_review_rollout_filename: Option<String>,
    include_windows_sandbox_log: bool,
    feedback_diagnostics: &FeedbackDiagnostics,
) -> super::SelectionViewParams
```

## Building the "Connectivity diagnostics" Section

The function builds `header_lines` (a vector of boxed `Renderable`), starting with an `"Upload logs?"` header and a list of files to be sent. It conditionally appends entries for the Windows sandbox log, the rollout path filename, the auto-review filename, and — when diagnostics aren't empty — a feedback diagnostics attachment file.

The connectivity section is gated by the `should_show_feedback_connectivity_details` helper. When true, it adds a blank line and a bold `"Connectivity diagnostics"` heading, then iterates over each diagnostic. For each one it pushes the `headline` prefixed with `"  - "`, then iterates the `details`, pushing each prefixed with `"    - "` and dimmed:

```rust
if should_show_feedback_connectivity_details(category, feedback_diagnostics) {
    header_lines.push(Line::from("").into());
    header_lines.push(Line::from("Connectivity diagnostics".bold()).into());
    for diagnostic in feedback_diagnostics.diagnostics() {
        header_lines
            .push(Line::from(vec!["  - ".into(), diagnostic.headline.clone().into()]).into());
        for detail in &diagnostic.details {
            header_lines.push(Line::from(vec!["    - ".dim(), detail.clone().into()]).into());
        }
    }
}
```

The returned `SelectionViewParams` includes a standard footer hint, "Yes"/"No" selection items (each carrying an action that sends an `OpenFeedbackNote` event with the appropriate `include_logs` value), and the assembled header wrapped in a `ColumnRenderable`.

## The `should_show` Helper

This returns true only for non-`GoodResult` categories that have non-empty diagnostics:

```rust
pub(crate) fn should_show_feedback_connectivity_details(
    category: FeedbackCategory,
    diagnostics: &FeedbackDiagnostics,
) -> bool {
    category != FeedbackCategory::GoodResult && !diagnostics.is_empty()
}
```

## How `intro_lines` Handles Diagnostics

Notably, the `FeedbackNoteView::intro_lines` method does **not** handle diagnostics at all. It ignores its `width` argument and simply returns a single line containing the gutter and the bold category title:

```rust
fn intro_lines(&self, _width: u16) -> Vec<Line<'static>> {
    let (title, _) = feedback_title_and_placeholder(self.category);
    vec![Line::from(vec![gutter(), title.bold()])]
}
```

So connectivity diagnostics appear only in the *upload consent* header (via `feedback_upload_consent_params`), not in the note view's intro lines.

